# Sales Commission Plan — FY26: commission earned

> Module Commission

This module encodes the quantum of commission earned for the Plan Year. The
decomposition follows the order in which the Plan itself builds the figure,
because that order is legislated rather than incidental: S-2.3 defines Net
Booked Revenue, S-2.2 turns it into Attainment against Quota, S-4 turns
Attainment into an accelerator, S-3.1 multiplies, and S-5 caps the product —
and S-5.2 says in terms that the cap comes last. Each step is a scope so that
an executed answer says which step produced which number.

Quota relief under S-6 is *upstream* of everything here: `QuotaRelief` computes
the Quota that `Attainment` divides by, and `QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief`
composes the two in the order S-6.2 fixes. Clawback under S-7 is *downstream*,
in `Clawback`. Neither is re-encoded here.

`Attainment` is carried as a `decimal`. Catala's percentage literals make that
exact and let the band tests be written with the same numerals the Plan uses:
`150%` is the decimal `1.5`, so `attainment_pct >= 150%` reads as S-4.1(d)
reads.

## Prologue — declarations

```catala-metadata
declaration enumeration TerminationReason:
  -- GrossMisconduct
  -- OtherReason

# A contract record as the revenue system holds it. `terminated_by_customer_on`
# and `not_renewed_at_first_renewal_on` are the two churn events S-2.4 names,
# absent where the event has not occurred. `customer_contract_dates` are the
# dates on which this customer held a contract with the Company, which is the
# history S-2.6 interrogates.
declaration structure Contract:
  data contract_id content integer
  data annual_contract_value content money
  data signature_date content date
  data terminated_by_customer_on content optional of date
  data not_renewed_at_first_renewal_on content optional of date
  data customer_contract_dates content list of date

declaration scope ChurnedContract:
  input contract content Contract
  output is_churned content boolean

declaration scope NewLogo:
  input signature_date content date
  input customer_contract_dates content list of date
  output window_start content date
  output is_new_logo content boolean

declaration scope AssignedQuota:
  input assigned_quota content money
  input commencement_date content date
  output quota_assignment_date content date
  output quota content money

declaration scope NetBookedRevenue:
  input contracts content list of Contract
  internal plan_year_contracts content list of Contract
  internal churned_contracts content list of Contract
  output gross_booked_revenue content money
  output churned_contract_value content money
  output net_booked_revenue content money
  output new_logo_revenue content money
  output new_logo_share content decimal

declaration scope Attainment:
  input net_booked_revenue content money
  input quota content decimal
  output attainment_pct content decimal

declaration scope Accelerator:
  input attainment_pct content decimal
  input new_logo_share content decimal
  input commencement_date content date
  output commenced_after_plan_year_start content boolean
  output s4_1_band content decimal
  output accelerator_before_joiner_cap content decimal
  output accelerator content decimal

declaration scope CommissionPayable:
  input net_booked_revenue content money
  input new_logo_share content decimal
  input quota content decimal
  input commencement_date content date
  input annual_base_salary content money
  output attainment_calc scope Attainment
  output accelerator_calc scope Accelerator
  output accelerator_base content money
  output commission_before_cap content money
  output cap content money
  output commission_payable content money

declaration scope LeaverCommission:
  input contracts content list of Contract
  input last_day_of_employment content date
  input termination_reason content TerminationReason
  input quota content decimal
  input commencement_date content date
  input annual_base_salary content money
  input commission_already_paid content money
  output qualifying_contracts content list of Contract
  output revenue scope NetBookedRevenue
  output entitlement scope CommissionPayable
  output commission_payable content money
  output overpaid_amount content money
```

## S-1 Introduction

| COMM-PLAN S-1.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:14)
|
| This Plan sets out the basis on which commission is earned by Employees
| in a quota-bearing sales role during the financial year commencing 1 October 2025
| and ending 30 September 2026 (the "Plan Year").

S-1.1 is the only place the Plan Year window is stated, so it is fixed here as
two constants and as the membership test every later clause ranges over. The
window is inclusive at both ends: the financial year *commences* on 1 October
2025 and *ends* on 30 September 2026, so a contract signed on either day is
signed during the Plan Year.

The block is `catala-metadata`, and so public, because S-6.1's relief is a
proration of this same window and `QuotaRelief` has to confine its day-counting
to it. A clause stated once in the Plan is encoded once and imported; the
alternative is a second copy of the window in another module, which is the
shape of defect this repo exists to prevent.

```catala-metadata
declaration plan_year_start content date equals |2025-10-01|
declaration plan_year_end content date equals |2026-09-30|

declaration signed_in_plan_year content boolean
  depends on c content Contract
  equals
    c.signature_date >= plan_year_start
    and c.signature_date <= plan_year_end
```

## S-2 Definitions

| COMM-PLAN S-2.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:26)
|
| "Quota" means the annual revenue target assigned to the Employee in
| writing at the start of the Plan Year, or on joining if later.

The computable content of S-2.1 is the as-of date of the assignment: the start
of the Plan Year, or the commencement date where that is later. The amount
itself is a written assignment and so is an input. `quota` is what
`QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota` reduces and what `Attainment` ultimately divides by.

```catala
scope AssignedQuota:
  definition quota_assignment_date equals
    Date.max of plan_year_start, commencement_date

  definition quota equals assigned_quota
```

| COMM-PLAN S-2.5 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:40)
|
| "Base Commission Rate" means 8.0% of Net Booked Revenue.

S-2.5 is worded as an amount ("8.0% of Net Booked Revenue") but S-3.1 uses the
Base Commission Rate as a *multiplier* of Net Booked Revenue. Read as an amount
it would make S-3.1 multiply revenue by an amount, which is not a quantity, so
the rate reading is the only coherent one and 8.0% is carried as the factor.

```catala
declaration base_commission_rate content decimal equals 8.0%
```

| COMM-PLAN S-2.4 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:36)
|
| "Churned Contract" means a contract which is terminated by the
| customer, or which is not renewed at its first renewal date, in either case
| within 180 days after its signature date.

Two limbs, disjunctive, each gated by the same 180-day window. "Within 180 days
after its signature date" is read inclusively — an event on the 180th day after
signature is within 180 days — and the window opens at signature, so an event
dated before signature is not a churn event at all. An event on day 181 is
outside, and the contract is not a Churned Contract however severe the churn.

```catala
scope ChurnedContract:
  definition is_churned equals
    (match contract.terminated_by_customer_on with pattern
     -- Absent: false
     -- Present content d:
         d >= contract.signature_date
         and d - contract.signature_date <= 180 day)
    or
    (match contract.not_renewed_at_first_renewal_on with pattern
     -- Absent: false
     -- Present content d:
         d >= contract.signature_date
         and d - contract.signature_date <= 180 day)
```

| COMM-PLAN S-2.6 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:42)
|
| "New Logo" means a customer which had no contract with the Company at
| any time in the 24 months preceding the signature date.

The window is the 24 months *preceding* the signature date, so it runs from
`signature_date - 24 month` inclusive up to, but not including, the signature
date itself: a contract cannot disqualify itself. The scope declares
`date round down` because 24 months back from 29 February lands on a date that
does not exist and Catala refuses to guess.

```catala
scope NewLogo:
  date round down

  definition window_start equals signature_date - 24 month

  definition is_new_logo equals
    not (exists d among customer_contract_dates such that
           d >= window_start and d < signature_date)
```

| COMM-PLAN S-2.3 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:32)
|
| "Net Booked Revenue" means the aggregate annual contract value of
| contracts signed by the Employee during the Plan Year, less the annual contract
| value of any Churned Contract.

Written as the clause writes it — an aggregate, less a deduction — rather than
as a filter, so that the two quantities the clause names are separately visible
on an answer.

```catala
scope NetBookedRevenue:
  definition plan_year_contracts equals
    list of c among contracts such that signed_in_plan_year of c

  definition churned_contracts equals
    list of c among plan_year_contracts
    such that (output of ChurnedContract with { -- contract: c }).is_churned

  definition gross_booked_revenue equals
    Money.sum of (map each c among plan_year_contracts to c.annual_contract_value)

  definition churned_contract_value equals
    Money.sum of (map each c among churned_contracts to c.annual_contract_value)

  definition net_booked_revenue equals
    gross_booked_revenue - churned_contract_value
```

| COMM-PLAN S-2.2 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:29)
|
| "Attainment" means Net Booked Revenue expressed as a percentage of
| Quota.

The `quota` supplied here must already be the S-6.1-relieved Quota, because
S-6.2 says relief is applied before Attainment is calculated. That is a
precondition on the input, and `QuotaRelief.CommissionAfterRelief` is the scope
that discharges it structurally: it takes the *assigned* Quota with the absence
records and can reach this scope only through `QuotaRelief.RelievedQuota`.
Calling `Attainment` or `CommissionPayable` with a bare `quota` is still
possible — the caller then carries the S-6.2 obligation itself.

**CE-0027.** The Quota is taken here as an exact `decimal` of pounds and not as
`money`, and that follows from S-6.2 read with S-6.1. The relieved Quota is the
assigned Quota less 1/365ths of it, so it is not in general a whole number of
pence: 30 days of relief on a £750,000 Quota leaves £688,356.1643835616....
Catala fixes `money` at the cent, so a `money` denominator here is that figure
rounded — and S-2.2 is the one place where rounding a denominator changes a
legal outcome, because the quotient it defines is what S-4.1 bands. On those
facts the rounded penny lifts Attainment from 49.99999968% to exactly 50.00%
and so moves the accelerator from S-4.1(a)'s 0.0 to S-4.1(b)'s 1.0, £27,534.25
on a £344,178.08 book. Nothing is lost by taking the ratio on the exact figure,
because S-2.2 makes Attainment a *percentage*: the relieved Quota is a target
and never a sum paid, and the only sum of money the Plan produces is S-3.1's
product, which is where the single conversion to `money` happens (CE-0015).
S-2.1's assigned Quota is still a sum of money assigned in writing, and
`AssignedQuota` above still carries it as one — the contrast is the point.

| COMM-PLAN S-2.2 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:29)
|
| "Attainment" means Net Booked Revenue expressed as a percentage of
| Quota.

**CE-0026.** The guard here used to be `assertion quota > $0`, and it was an
over-tight one. S-6.1 can plainly produce a nil Quota: an Employee absent on
long-term sickness absence for every day of the Plan Year has her Quota reduced
by 1/365th of it 365 times, which is the whole of it. The guard therefore
refused an input the Plan itself compels, and it did not even prevent the
mischief it was aimed at — Catala is not lazy, so the quotient was evaluated
and raised a division by zero before any assertion could refuse anything, which
turned a lawful question into a crash.

Where the Quota is nil the Plan answers without S-2.2 at all. S-3.1 computes
commission as Net Booked Revenue multiplied by the Base Commission Rate
multiplied by the S-4 accelerator, and on the only facts that reduce a Quota to
nil Net Booked Revenue is nil too, so the product is nil whatever the
accelerator and S-5.1's cap cannot bite. The nil-Quota limb accordingly reports
Attainment of 0%, which is the reading that asserts the least — no attainment
of a target that has itself been reduced to nothing — and which cannot change
the answer, because the multiplicand S-4.2 fixes is itself nil.

What survives of the old guard is two assertions, each a bound the Plan states
rather than a programming convenience. A Quota cannot be negative: S-2.1 makes
it an assigned annual revenue target, and S-6.1's reduction is "1/365th ... for
each day" of a 365-day year and so cannot exceed the annual Quota. And a nil
Quota can only reach this scope alongside nil Net Booked Revenue: the Plan's
only route to one is a qualifying absence covering every day of the Plan Year,
and an Employee absent on all of them signs no contract during it, so S-2.3's
aggregate is nil. A positive Net Booked Revenue against a nil Quota is not a
percentage of anything and the Plan fixes no answer for it, so the scope
declines it rather than inventing a band.

The second limb's condition is `quota <= 0.0` rather than `= 0.0` so that the
two limbs are exhaustive over the type and the refusal of a negative Quota is
made by the assertion, which states the bound and says why, instead of by the
absence of any applicable rule, whose diagnostic says neither. Nothing but nil
survives the assertion, so the limb answers only for the nil Quota S-6.1
produces.

```catala
scope Attainment:
  label s2_2 definition attainment_pct
    under condition quota > 0.0
    consequence equals (decimal of net_booked_revenue) / quota

  label s2_2 definition attainment_pct
    under condition quota <= 0.0
    consequence equals 0.0

  assertion quota >= 0.0
  assertion (quota > 0.0) or (net_booked_revenue = $0)
```

## S-3 Commission calculation

| COMM-PLAN S-3.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:47)
|
| Commission is calculated as Net Booked Revenue multiplied by the Base
| Commission Rate, multiplied by the accelerator determined under S-4.

The multiplicand is `accelerator_base`, which S-4.2 below fixes as the whole of
Net Booked Revenue, and the accelerator is the one the `Accelerator` sub-scope
determines — that is, after S-4.3 and S-4.4 have had their effect. This product
is pre-cap: S-5 operates on it, never on any part of it.

S-3.1 prescribes *one* product of three factors, and it is computed as one.
Catala fixes the precision of `money` at the cent, so a `money`-typed
intermediate is rounded there: multiplying Net Booked Revenue by the Base
Commission Rate first produced a rounded sum of money which the accelerator then
magnified. On Net Booked Revenue of $10,000.44 that paid $1,200.06 where S-3.1's
product, $10,000.44 x 0.08 x 1.5 = $1,200.0528, is $1,200.05 (CE-0015). The
error is systematic across accelerators — half a cent at the first step becomes
0.75 of a cent at 1.5, a whole cent at 2.0 — and S-2.5 gives no warrant for the
intermediate: it defines the Base Commission Rate as a rate to be applied, not
as a separately payable sum, and S-5.1 caps this figure rather than rebuilding
it, so the discrepancy survives into what is paid. The product is therefore
carried as an exact `decimal` — Catala decimals are exact rationals, not floats
— and converted to `money` once, at the end, which is the only point at which
the Plan produces a sum of money.

```catala
scope CommissionPayable:
  definition commission_before_cap equals
    money of
      (decimal of accelerator_base
       * base_commission_rate
       * accelerator_calc.accelerator)
```

## S-4 Accelerators

| COMM-PLAN S-4.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:52)
|
| The accelerator is determined by Attainment as follows:
|
|   (a) Attainment of less than 50%: accelerator of 0.0;
|   (b) Attainment of 50% or more but less than 100%: accelerator of 1.0;
|   (c) Attainment of 100% or more but less than 150%: accelerator of 1.5;
|   (d) Attainment of 150% or more: accelerator of 2.0.

Four mutually exclusive limbs, so they share one label and form a single base
node. Both bounds of each band are written out rather than collapsed into an
if-else chain: the Plan's operators are "or more" (inclusive) at the bottom of
a band and "less than" (exclusive) at the top, and 100% therefore belongs to
band (c), not to band (b). The band value is kept as its own variable
`s4_1_band` because S-4.3 increases "the accelerator determined under S-4.1",
which requires that value to remain available after S-4.3 has defeated it.

The root of the `accelerator` chain is unconditional — the four bands are
exhaustive over the reals — so the exceptions below have no parent condition to
repeat.

```catala
scope Accelerator:
  label s4_1_table definition s4_1_band
    under condition attainment_pct < 50%
    consequence equals 0.0

  label s4_1_table definition s4_1_band
    under condition attainment_pct > 50% and attainment_pct < 100%
    consequence equals 1.0

  label s4_1_table definition s4_1_band
    under condition attainment_pct >= 100% and attainment_pct < 150%
    consequence equals 1.5

  label s4_1_table definition s4_1_band
    under condition attainment_pct >= 150%
    consequence equals 2.0

  label s4_1 definition accelerator equals s4_1_band
```

| COMM-PLAN S-4.2 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:59)
|
| The accelerator determined under S-4.1 applies to the whole of Net
| Booked Revenue and not only to the portion above the relevant threshold.

S-4.1 is a cliff, not a marginal rate, and S-4.2 is the clause that says so.
The base to which the accelerator applies is therefore named here, and the
definition is an identity precisely because the clause rejects the marginal
alternative: it is *not* `net_booked_revenue - band_threshold`. Encoding S-4.1
as a tiered rate would understate commission for every attainer above 50%, so
the choice is kept visible as a quantity rather than buried in S-3.1's product.

```catala
scope CommissionPayable:
  definition accelerator_base equals net_booked_revenue
```

| COMM-PLAN S-4.3 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:62)
|
| By way of exception to S-4.1, where more than 60% of Net Booked Revenue
| is attributable to New Logo customers, the accelerator determined under S-4.1 is
| increased by 0.25.

The share S-4.3 tests is measured against Net Booked Revenue — that is, after
the S-2.3 churn deduction — so a churned contract counts in neither numerator
nor denominator. The guard for a nil Net Booked Revenue is needed because
Catala is not lazy and the quotient is computed whether or not S-4.3 fires.

```catala
scope NetBookedRevenue:
  definition new_logo_revenue equals
    Money.sum of (map each c among plan_year_contracts
                  such that
                    not (output of ChurnedContract with { -- contract: c }).is_churned
                    and (output of NewLogo with {
                           -- signature_date: c.signature_date
                           -- customer_contract_dates: c.customer_contract_dates
                         }).is_new_logo
                  to c.annual_contract_value)

  definition new_logo_share equals
    if net_booked_revenue = $0 then 0.0
    else new_logo_revenue / net_booked_revenue
```

| COMM-PLAN S-4.3 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:62)
|
| By way of exception to S-4.1, where more than 60% of Net Booked Revenue
| is attributable to New Logo customers, the accelerator determined under S-4.1 is
| increased by 0.25.

The rate limb of the same clause. "More than 60%" is strict, so a share of
exactly 60% attracts no uplift. `accelerator_before_joiner_cap` holds the
combined S-4.1-and-S-4.3 figure, which is what S-4.4 caps.

```catala
scope Accelerator:
  definition accelerator_before_joiner_cap equals
    if new_logo_share > 60% then s4_1_band + 0.25 else s4_1_band

  label s4_3 exception s4_1 definition accelerator
    under condition new_logo_share > 60%
    consequence equals accelerator_before_joiner_cap
```

| COMM-PLAN S-4.4 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:66)
|
| By way of exception to S-4.1 and S-4.3, the accelerator applicable to an
| Employee who commenced employment after the start of the Plan Year is capped at
| 1.5 for the Plan Year in which they commenced.

An exception to *both* S-4.1 and S-4.3, so it sits below `s4_3` in the chain
and thereby defeats either. Its condition is the joiner test alone: it must
*not* repeat S-4.3's New Logo condition, because S-4.4 applies to a mid-year
joiner whether or not the uplift was earned — repeating it would leave a joiner
with a 30% New Logo share on the uncapped 2.0. The value capped is
`accelerator_before_joiner_cap`, so the cap bites on the S-4.3 figure where
S-4.3 applied and on the bare S-4.1 band where it did not, and is inert where
the otherwise applicable accelerator is already 1.5 or below.

"For the Plan Year in which they commenced" identifies the Plan Year this
module encodes, so the test is the literal one S-4.4 states. It is not
narrowed to commencement *within* the window: an employee who commenced after
30 September 2026 commenced in a later Plan Year, but could have signed no
contract during this one, so Net Booked Revenue, Attainment and the whole S-3
product are nil for them whichever accelerator is selected.

```catala
scope Accelerator:
  definition commenced_after_plan_year_start equals
    commencement_date > plan_year_start

  label s4_4 exception s4_3 definition accelerator
    under condition commenced_after_plan_year_start
    consequence equals Decimal.min of accelerator_before_joiner_cap, 1.5
```

## S-5 Caps

| COMM-PLAN S-5.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:72)
|
| Total commission payable to an Employee in respect of the Plan Year
| must not exceed 250% of the Employee's annual base salary.

The base ceiling, and the constraint it imposes stated as an assertion so that
"must not exceed" is checked rather than merely implemented.

```catala
scope CommissionPayable:
  label s5_1 definition cap equals annual_base_salary * 250%

  assertion commission_payable <= cap
```

| COMM-PLAN S-5.3 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:78)
|
| By way of exception to S-5.1, where the Employee's Attainment exceeds
| 200%, the cap is 400% of annual base salary.

An exception to S-5.1, encoded as one. "Exceeds 200%" is strict — unlike
S-4.1(d)'s "150% or more" — so Attainment of exactly 200% keeps the 250% cap.
S-5.1's own definition is unconditional, so there is no parent condition to
repeat here.

```catala
scope CommissionPayable:
  label s5_3 exception s5_1 definition cap
    under condition attainment_calc.attainment_pct > 200%
    consequence equals annual_base_salary * 400%
```

| COMM-PLAN S-5.2 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:75)
|
| The cap in S-5.1 is applied after the accelerator under S-4 and after
| any adjustment under S-6.

S-5.2 has computational content, not merely commentary: it names the operand
the cap is applied to. That operand is `commission_before_cap`, which already
embeds the S-4 accelerator; and the accelerator is computed from an Attainment
whose denominator is the Quota supplied by `Quota_relief`, so the S-6 adjustment
is upstream too. The wiring below is the order of operations, made structural
so that a caller cannot cap an earlier quantity: capping revenue-times-rate and
then accelerating gives a materially different — and larger — figure, which is
what S-5.2 forbids.

```catala
scope CommissionPayable:
  definition attainment_calc.net_booked_revenue equals net_booked_revenue
  definition attainment_calc.quota equals quota

  definition accelerator_calc.attainment_pct equals attainment_calc.attainment_pct
  definition accelerator_calc.new_logo_share equals new_logo_share
  definition accelerator_calc.commencement_date equals commencement_date

  definition commission_payable equals
    Money.min of commission_before_cap, cap
```

## S-8 Leavers

| COMM-PLAN S-8.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:106)
|
| An Employee who ceases employment is entitled to commission in respect
| of contracts signed on or before their last day of employment, payable in the
| ordinary payment cycle.

"On or before" is inclusive, so a contract signed on the last day of employment
qualifies. The qualifying contracts are fed to `NetBookedRevenue`, so S-2.3's
churn deduction and the whole S-3 to S-5 computation apply to them unchanged —
S-8.1 narrows the population of contracts and changes nothing else. What is
payable is the entitlement less what has already been paid.

That figure is floored at nil, and the floor is part of what S-8.1 confers
rather than a rule defeating it: the clause creates an entitlement running one
way only — a sum payable *to* the Employee in the ordinary payment cycle — which
is exhausted, not reversed, once what has been paid equals it. The Plan's only
provision that can make a sum run the other way is S-7.1, and it operates only
where commission was paid on a contract that has become a Churned Contract
within S-2.4, only over the commission attributable to that contract, only at
the Company's option, and subject to the S-7.2 material-breach bar and the
S-7.3 24-month long-stop. Absent a Churned Contract none of that can even be
tested, so the negative figure this scope used to report asserted a debt the
Plan does not create (CE-0016).

```catala
scope LeaverCommission:
  definition qualifying_contracts equals
    list of c among contracts
    such that c.signature_date <= last_day_of_employment

  definition revenue.contracts equals qualifying_contracts

  definition entitlement.net_booked_revenue equals revenue.net_booked_revenue
  definition entitlement.new_logo_share equals revenue.new_logo_share
  definition entitlement.quota equals quota
  definition entitlement.commencement_date equals commencement_date
  definition entitlement.annual_base_salary equals annual_base_salary

  label s8_1 definition commission_payable equals
    Money.positive of
      (entitlement.commission_payable - commission_already_paid)
```

| COMM-PLAN S-8.1 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:106)
|
| An Employee who ceases employment is entitled to commission in respect
| of contracts signed on or before their last day of employment, payable in the
| ordinary payment cycle.

S-8.2 below confirms that this field means "amount payable to the Employee" and
not a net balance: it returns $0 for a gross-misconduct leaver rather than the
negative of the sum already paid. The floor is written into the S-8.1 expression
rather than added as an exception to it, because an exception would be a sibling
of `s8_2` and the two would conflict for an overpaid gross-misconduct leaver.

The excess is not discarded, only denied the status of a payable: it is reported
as `overpaid_amount`, so an answer can state the fact without asserting a right.
The Plan confers no recovery power over that sum — S-7 is the only recovery
power in the instrument and it is unavailable absent a Churned Contract — and
whether it is recoverable on some other footing is a question this Plan does not
answer.

```catala
scope LeaverCommission:
  definition overpaid_amount equals
    Money.positive of
      (commission_already_paid - entitlement.commission_payable)
```

| COMM-PLAN S-8.2 (003-sales-commission-plan.md:110)
|
| By way of exception to S-8.1, an Employee whose employment is terminated
| for gross misconduct forfeits any commission not yet paid at the date of
| termination.

What is forfeited is the unpaid balance, which is exactly the quantity S-8.1
defines, so the exception zeroes it. `s8_1` is unconditional, so there is no
parent condition to repeat. The gross misconduct finding is made by the
disciplinary process and reaches the scope as a recorded termination reason;
it is not a judgement the scope makes.

```catala
scope LeaverCommission:
  label s8_2 exception s8_1 definition commission_payable
    under condition termination_reason with pattern GrossMisconduct
    consequence equals $0
```
